**Current versus accepted.** Alpha emits HTML from root activity and expects a
homepage at the entry root. The accepted design keeps directory routes but
requires explicit root-only `$page` pages and command-specific no-page rules.

### Directory routes

Routes come from directory position, not from the `@` filename:

[codeblock, $code("text"):
    src/@page.moth       -> index.html
    src/about/@module.moth -> about/index.html
]

The root filename is cosmetic. An ordinary file and `index.moth` have no page
meaning.

### Page and command rules

After the cutover, a normal root needs an explicit page purpose:

[codeblock, $code("moth"):
    $page
]

`check` accepts a valid zero-page project but still rejects unpurposed
runtime work. HTML `build` and `dev` need a page somewhere below `entry_root`,
not necessarily at its root. Single-file HTML output requires `$page` on its
synthetic root. A metadata-only page still emits a complete document.

The builder does not invent a homepage or scan arbitrary `.moth` files.
Generated `dev/` and `release/` folders remain output, not source.
